Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Missing permission checks in MediaQualityService Binder methods allowed unprivileged applications to read signature-gated TYPE_SYSTEM picture and sound profiles. This could leak sensitive device configuration parameters and unique UUIDs.

This commit adds MANAGE_GLOBAL_PICTURE_QUALITY_SERVICE and MANAGE_GLOBAL_SOUND_QUALITY_SERVICE permission checks (via `hasGlobalPictureQualityServicePermission` and `hasGlobalSoundQualityServicePermission`) to several Binder methods in `MediaQualityService`. If an unauthorized caller attempts to access these profiles, the service now logs an error, sends an error notification, and returns safe default values (such as an empty list, `-1`, or `null`) to prevent the information leak.

Bug: 514738573
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Test: gambit

Change-Id: Ic8d9f4472b4a1c114aa105491c4f7182e5c47de9

(cherry picked from commit cd2700182d5102c63976a6ecc0cc3f13594f64c7)
